A Docker image is built from a series of filesystem layers.

Each Dockerfile instruction that changes the filesystem can contribute a layer to the resulting image.

Conceptually:
┌──────────────────────────┐
│ Application source code  │ ← Layer
├──────────────────────────┤
│ npm dependencies         │ ← Layer
├──────────────────────────┤
│ Node.js / base files     │ ← Layer
├──────────────────────────┤
│ Base image               │ ← Layer
└──────────────────────────┘